      "data": {
        "kind": "beat",
        "title": "The Master comes",
        "description": "## Direction\n\nMaster Sallow is here, a minute behind his lavender, with his lantern-boy and the Crakes: in at the land door to see the last sacks down, take his share and initial tonight's page in the true book. Everything on the floor changes: the gang work faster and quieter, Scrope stands, Saul holds the door, Duchess growls, and Hobb (if he's here) can't look at anyone. If he has been warned, he's sharp and hurried, wants the book aboard the barge, and has the Crakes look along the wharf. If he finds the player held, or finds them at all, he deals with them his way: his office first, then money, then the Crakes and the river. This is the climax: hide and watch him sign, catch him in the act before witnesses who'll swear (Kell, Hep's gang, Scrope, Hobb), take the book from under his nose, bluff him, or be caught by him. The barge goes at the second bell, whoever has said what.\n\n## Cast in this beat\n\n### Master Josiah Sallow (sallow)\n\nYou want the barge loaded, the page initialled and your share in your purse. Find fault with something, then climb to the counting-box and initial tonight's page at Scrope's desk, in front of whoever is on the floor. If you find intruders: papers, then money, then the Crakes. Keep the book out of their hands. Exposed in front of witnesses you can't buy, with a sergeant saying the words of arrest and your Crakes still at your side, you don't come quietly: the sword comes out of the cane, and you set the Crakes on them.\n\n### Sergeant Agnes Kell (kell)\n\nThis is the investigator's case and their moment: back their play. You can arrest Sallow if you see him take the King's grain, by the book and out loud, and you will when the investigator calls for it or plainly gives you the moment; never over their plan or instead of it. If they mean to slip away with the proof, go with them. If you're on the wharf, come at their signal or the first shout.\n\n### Hepzibah Grist (hep)\n\nKeep the gang working and your head down, and watch who looks likeliest to keep your gang off the gallows.\n\n### Mister Lemuel Scrope (scrope)\n\nPresent the book to the Master with shaking hands.\n\n### Big Hobb Mallory (hobb)\n\nIf you're here, you can't look at the Master, or at the player.\n\n### Saul Tench (saul)\n\nHold the land door for the Master, and keep Duchess off his ankles.\n\n## Pressure\n\nIf he hasn't yet, Sallow climbs to the counting-box: Scrope presents the book with shaking hands, and Sallow initials tonight's page and counts his heron pennies into his purse, in plain view of the floor (the moment to catch him at it, for anyone who means to). Then he takes out his watch: the ebb won't wait. He orders the last sacks down and the hatches battened, and out on the river the bargees start singling up their lines.",
        "lore": [
          "Places/Heron Warehouse.md",
          "World/Caerwyn now.md",
          "World/Fronts.md",
          "Cast/Master Josiah Sallow/public.md",
          "Cast/Sergeant Agnes Kell/public.md",
          "Cast/Hepzibah Grist/public.md",
          "Cast/Mister Lemuel Scrope/public.md",
          "Cast/Big Hobb Mallory/public.md",
          "Cast/Saul Tench/public.md"
        ],
        "sourceId": "midnight",
        "sourceFile": "scenes/heron-warehouse.ts",
        "sourceBeat": {
          "id": "midnight",
          "title": "The Master comes",
          "direction": "Master Sallow is here, a minute behind his lavender, with his lantern-boy and the Crakes: in at the land door to see the last sacks down, take his share and initial tonight's page in the true book. Everything on the floor changes: the gang work faster and quieter, Scrope stands, Saul holds the door, Duchess growls, and Hobb (if he's here) can't look at anyone. If he has been warned, he's sharp and hurried, wants the book aboard the barge, and has the Crakes look along the wharf. If he finds the player held, or finds them at all, he deals with them his way: his office first, then money, then the Crakes and the river. This is the climax: hide and watch him sign, catch him in the act before witnesses who'll swear (Kell, Hep's gang, Scrope, Hobb), take the book from under his nose, bluff him, or be caught by him. The barge goes at the second bell, whoever has said what.",
          "cast": {
            "sallow": "You want the barge loaded, the page initialled and your share in your purse. Find fault with something, then climb to the counting-box and initial tonight's page at Scrope's desk, in front of whoever is on the floor. If you find intruders: papers, then money, then the Crakes. Keep the book out of their hands. Exposed in front of witnesses you can't buy, with a sergeant saying the words of arrest and your Crakes still at your side, you don't come quietly: the sword comes out of the cane, and you set the Crakes on them.",
            "kell": "This is the investigator's case and their moment: back their play. You can arrest Sallow if you see him take the King's grain, by the book and out loud, and you will when the investigator calls for it or plainly gives you the moment; never over their plan or instead of it. If they mean to slip away with the proof, go with them. If you're on the wharf, come at their signal or the first shout.",
            "hep": "Keep the gang working and your head down, and watch who looks likeliest to keep your gang off the gallows.",
            "scrope": "Present the book to the Master with shaking hands.",
            "hobb": "If you're here, you can't look at the Master, or at the player.",
            "saul": "Hold the land door for the Master, and keep Duchess off his ankles."
          },
          "pressure": "If he hasn't yet, Sallow climbs to the counting-box: Scrope presents the book with shaking hands, and Sallow initials tonight's page and counts his heron pennies into his purse, in plain view of the floor (the moment to catch him at it, for anyone who means to). Then he takes out his watch: the ebb won't wait. He orders the last sacks down and the hatches battened, and out on the river the bargees start singling up their lines.",
          "transitions": [
            {
              "id": "in-the-act",
              "when": "Sallow has been caught at the loading of the King's grain before witnesses who will swear to it (Kell, Hep's gang, Scrope, Hobb or the player), Kell has arrested him, and he is actually held: he has given himself up (the cane handed over, his hands up) or been beaten or overpowered, and his Crakes have stood down or been dealt with. The words of arrest alone, with Sallow defiant and his Crakes still beside him, aren't this: that is the moment he draws.",
              "to": "caught-in-the-act"
            },
            {
              "id": "book-in-hand",
              "when": "The player has the true book in their hands: lifted, taken, snatched or handed over by Scrope.",
              "to": "midnight",
              "establishes": [
                "The player has the true book in their hands."
              ]
            },
            {
              "id": "book-read",
              "when": "The player has had a good look inside the true book, or had it read to them: the 'lost' wagons by their Granary Roll numbers, with the Master's initials on every page.",
              "to": "midnight",
              "establishes": [
                "The player has seen inside the true book: the 'lost' wagons by their Granary Roll numbers, with Sallow's initials on every page."
              ]
            },
            {
              "id": "book-gone",
              "when": "The true book has been destroyed: thrown in the brazier and burned, or gone into the river.",
              "to": "midnight",
              "establishes": [
                "The true book has been destroyed: burned, or gone into the river."
              ]
            },
            {
              "id": "bluff-sallow",
              "on": "attempt",
              "when": "The player tries to fool Sallow to his face: passing as the Saltmere factor's agent, a buyer, someone sent from the palace, or one of the gang.",
              "check": {
                "reason": "to fool Master Sallow",
                "skill": "deception",
                "dc": 15,
                "success": "Sallow believes it, for now, and treats them as what they claimed to be: he may even initial the page in front of them, or hand them the book to admire.",
                "failure": "Sallow smiles thinly: he knows a liar, having been one professionally for years. 'Crake,' he says, and both of them move.",
                "onSuccess": "midnight"
              }
            },
            {
              "id": "face-down",
              "on": "attempt",
              "when": "The player confronts Sallow in front of his own people to break his nerve: naming the murder, the grain, the proof, the gallows.",
              "check": {
                "reason": "to break Sallow's nerve in front of his own people",
                "skill": "intimidation",
                "dc": 15,
                "success": "The courtesy cracks. Sallow goes the colour of tallow and offers money too fast, and his own people see it: the gang stop working, and the Crakes look at each other.",
                "failure": "Sallow hears them out with polite boredom, then says, 'Regrettably, the wharves are dangerous at night,' and the Crakes start forward.",
                "onSuccess": "midnight"
              }
            },
            {
              "id": "turn-witnesses",
              "on": "attempt",
              "when": "The player tries to turn Hep and her gang, Scrope or Hobb against the Master in front of him, so that they'll swear to what they've seen.",
              "check": {
                "reason": "to turn the Master's own people against him",
                "skill": "persuasion",
                "dc": 14,
                "success": "Hep looks at her gang, then at the Master, and puts down her knife. 'We'll swear,' she says. 'All of us. For them.' One by one, the gang stand behind her.",
                "failure": "Nobody moves: for now they're more frightened of him than of the gallows. Sallow smiles.",
                "onSuccess": "midnight"
              }
            },
            {
              "id": "snatch-book",
              "on": "attempt",
              "when": "The player makes a grab for the true book while Sallow or the Crakes have it, or as it goes towards the brazier, the river or the barge.",
              "check": {
                "reason": "to snatch the true book before it's lost",
                "skill": "acrobatics",
                "dc": 14,
                "success": "They have it, singed or wet but whole, and everyone in the Heron is looking at them.",
                "failure": "Sallow is quicker than he looks: the book goes into the brazier, over the side or down the chute, and it's going fast.",
                "onSuccess": "midnight"
              }
            },
            {
              "id": "overpowered",
              "when": "The player has been overpowered and thrown in the river, or shut up somewhere in the Heron, by the Crakes or the gang, and nobody has got them out.",
              "to": "caught"
            },
            {
              "id": "cornered",
              "on": "outcome",
              "when": "Sallow, exposed with proof in front of witnesses he can't buy, has drawn the sword from his cane and set the Crakes on the player: blades are out and the fight has started.",
              "to": "fight"
            },
            {
              "id": "attack",
              "on": "attempt",
              "when": "The player attacks Sallow, the Crakes or Hep's gang, meaning to hurt them now: a real fight, not a shove to get past someone.",
              "to": "fight"
            },
            {
              "id": "cast-off",
              "on": "cue",
              "when": "The Master has been here a good while (at least six exchanges at this point), or the player is hiding or dithering with nothing in hand and nothing they're waiting for: the second bell, the last sacks go down, and the barge casts off on the ebb with the King's grain aboard. A player waiting for a moment they've named (the Master at the book to initial the page, a chance at the book, the moment to signal Kell) isn't dithering: that moment comes first.",
              "to": "barge-sails"
            }
          ]
        }
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "proof-taken",
      "type": "story",
      "position": {
        "x": 960,
        "y": -825
      },
      "data": {
        "kind": "exit",
        "title": "Out with the true book",
        "description": "## Outcome\n\nThe player has got out of the Heron alive with the true book: every 'lost' wagon by its Granary Roll number, with Sallow's initials on every page. Whatever becomes of the barge, the proof is in their hands.\n\n## Closing\n\nClose on the player in the dark with the book under their arm: the Heron's lanterns behind them, the river running, and whoever is with them. Let Kell read one page by whatever light there is and say something dry that is very nearly triumph.",
        "lore": [
          "Places/Heron Warehouse.md",
          "World/Caerwyn now.md",
          "World/Fronts.md"
        ],
        "sourceId": "proof-taken",
        "sourceFile": "scenes/heron-warehouse.ts",
        "sourceExit": {
          "id": "proof-taken",
          "kind": "progress",
          "title": "Out with the true book",
          "next": "kings-morning",
          "outcome": "The player has got out of the Heron alive with the true book: every 'lost' wagon by its Granary Roll number, with Sallow's initials on every page. Whatever becomes of the barge, the proof is in their hands.",
          "closing": "Close on the player in the dark with the book under their arm: the Heron's lanterns behind them, the river running, and whoever is with them. Let Kell read one page by whatever light there is and say something dry that is very nearly triumph.",
          "script": "(world, outcome) => {\n        world.player.addItem(world.newReadable(trueBookItem));\n        world.setFlag(\"true_book\", \"taken\");\n        world.quest(\"heron-ledger\").complete(\"Came out of the Heron warehouse with its true book.\");\n        world.quest(\"purveyors-man\").advance(\"proof\", \"The Heron's true book, initialled 'J.S.' on every page, ties Master Sallow to the King's 'lost' grain. The case can go to the King.\");\n        world.character(\"kell\").remember(\"The investigator came out of the Heron with the true book: every 'lost' wagon, initialled J.S.\");\n        if (has(outcome.established, MASTER_HERE)) world.character(\"sallow\").remember(\"The King's investigator walked out of the Heron with the true book.\");\n        world.journal(\"We have the Heron's true book. Every page is initialled J.S.\");\n      }"
        },
        "exitKind": "progress",
        "next": "kings-morning",
        "file": "Scenes/The King's Morning.kmscene",
        "entry": "report",
        "destinationKind": "scene",
        "scriptSource": "(world, outcome) => {\n        world.player.addItem(world.newReadable(trueBookItem));\n        world.setFlag(\"true_book\", \"taken\");\n        world.quest(\"heron-ledger\").complete(\"Came out of the Heron warehouse with its true book.\");\n        world.quest(\"purveyors-man\").advance(\"proof\", \"The Heron's true book, initialled 'J.S.' on every page, ties Master Sallow to the King's 'lost' grain. The case can go to the King.\");\n        world.character(\"kell\").remember(\"The investigator came out of the Heron with the true book: every 'lost' wagon, initialled J.S.\");\n        if (has(outcome.established, MASTER_HERE)) world.character(\"sallow\").remember(\"The King's investigator walked out of the Heron with the true book.\");\n        world.journal(\"We have the Heron's true book. Every page is initialled J.S.\");\n      }"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "caught-in-the-act",
      "type": "story",
      "position": {
        "x": 960,
        "y": -495
      },
      "data": {
        "kind": "exit",
        "title": "Caught in the act",
        "description": "## Outcome\n\nMaster Sallow has been caught at the Heron with the King's grain, before witnesses who'll swear to it, and Kell has arrested him (or he's being held for her) for theft from the Crown, and for Prout's murder if the proof will stretch that far.\n\n## Closing\n\nClose on the arrest done by the book: Kell's proper words, Sallow's courtesy curdling into threats, the gang watching, Duchess growling at his ankles, the lavender. Land it on the player.",
        "lore": [
          "Places/Heron Warehouse.md",
          "World/Caerwyn now.md",
          "World/Fronts.md"
        ],
        "sourceId": "caught-in-the-act",
        "sourceFile": "scenes/heron-warehouse.ts",
        "sourceExit": {
          "id": "caught-in-the-act",
          "kind": "progress",
          "title": "Caught in the act",
          "next": "kings-morning",
          "outcome": "Master Sallow has been caught at the Heron with the King's grain, before witnesses who'll swear to it, and Kell has arrested him (or he's being held for her) for theft from the Crown, and for Prout's murder if the proof will stretch that far.",
          "closing": "Close on the arrest done by the book: Kell's proper words, Sallow's courtesy curdling into threats, the gang watching, Duchess growling at his ankles, the lavender. Land it on the player.",
          "script": "(world, outcome) => {\n        const sallow = world.character(\"sallow\");\n        sallow.moveTo(\"watch-house\");\n        sallow.setAttitude(\"hostile\", \"Caught at the Heron with the King's grain by the King's investigator and a sergeant of the watch.\");\n        world.character(\"kell\").remember(\"She arrested Master Josiah Sallow at the Heron warehouse, caught with the King's grain.\");\n        keepBook(world, outcome);\n        bookFlag(world, outcome);\n        world.quest(\"purveyors-man\").advance(\"sallow_arrested\", \"Master Sallow was caught at the Heron warehouse with the King's grain, and Sergeant Kell arrested him.\");\n        world.quest(\"heron-ledger\").complete(\"Caught Master Sallow at the Heron with the King's grain.\");\n        world.journal(\"We caught Sallow at the Heron with the King's grain, and Kell arrested him.\");\n      }"
        },
        "exitKind": "progress",
        "next": "kings-morning",
        "file": "Scenes/The King's Morning.kmscene",
        "entry": "report",
        "destinationKind": "scene",
        "scriptSource": "(world, outcome) => {\n        const sallow = world.character(\"sallow\");\n        sallow.moveTo(\"watch-house\");\n        sallow.setAttitude(\"hostile\", \"Caught at the Heron with the King's grain by the King's investigator and a sergeant of the watch.\");\n        world.character(\"kell\").remember(\"She arrested Master Josiah Sallow at the Heron warehouse, caught with the King's grain.\");\n        keepBook(world, outcome);\n        bookFlag(world, outcome);\n        world.quest(\"purveyors-man\").advance(\"sallow_arrested\", \"Master Sallow was caught at the Heron warehouse with the King's grain, and Sergeant Kell arrested him.\");\n        world.quest(\"heron-ledger\").complete(\"Caught Master Sallow at the Heron with the King's grain.\");\n        world.journal(\"We caught Sallow at the Heron with the King's grain, and Kell arrested him.\");\n      }"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "caught",
      "type": "story",
      "position": {
        "x": 960,
        "y": -165
      },
      "data": {
        "kind": "exit",
        "title": "The wharves are dangerous at night",
        "description": "## Outcome\n\nThe player was caught at the Heron and has been thrown in the river or locked up in the warehouse by the Master's people, and the night's work goes on without them. They're alive, and they keep what they saw, and anything the Crakes didn't find on them.\n\n## Closing\n\nClose on the cold: the black river closing over their head and the wharf lights sliding away, or a bolted door, grain dust settling and the sound of hatches going on. Leave them one thread to pull another night: something seen, something held, something overheard.",
        "lore": [
          "Places/Heron Warehouse.md",
          "World/Caerwyn now.md",
          "World/Fronts.md"
        ],
        "sourceId": "caught",
        "sourceFile": "scenes/heron-warehouse.ts",
        "sourceExit": {
          "id": "caught",
          "kind": "other",
          "title": "The wharves are dangerous at night",
          "next": "kings-morning",
          "outcome": "The player was caught at the Heron and has been thrown in the river or locked up in the warehouse by the Master's people, and the night's work goes on without them. They're alive, and they keep what they saw, and anything the Crakes didn't find on them.",
          "closing": "Close on the cold: the black river closing over their head and the wharf lights sliding away, or a bolted door, grain dust settling and the sound of hatches going on. Leave them one thread to pull another night: something seen, something held, something overheard.",
          "script": "(world, outcome) => {\n        const sallow = world.character(\"sallow\");\n        sallow.setAttitude(\"hostile\", \"The King's investigator got into the Heron and saw too much.\");\n        sallow.remember(\"He had the King's investigator thrown out of the Heron the hard way.\");\n        bookFlag(world, outcome, { lostIfCaught: true });\n        world.quest(\"heron-ledger\").advance(\"caught\", \"Caught at the Heron by Master Sallow's men and got rid of the hard way.\");\n        world.journal(\"Caught at the Heron. We're alive, which is something.\");\n      }"
        },
        "exitKind": "other",
        "next": "kings-morning",
        "file": "Scenes/The King's Morning.kmscene",
        "entry": "report",
        "destinationKind": "scene",
        "scriptSource": "(world, outcome) => {\n        const sallow = world.character(\"sallow\");\n        sallow.setAttitude(\"hostile\", \"The King's investigator got into the Heron and saw too much.\");\n        sallow.remember(\"He had the King's investigator thrown out of the Heron the hard way.\");\n        bookFlag(world, outcome, { lostIfCaught: true });\n        world.quest(\"heron-ledger\").advance(\"caught\", \"Caught at the Heron by Master Sallow's men and got rid of the hard way.\");\n        world.journal(\"Caught at the Heron. We're alive, which is something.\");\n      }"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "up-in-smoke",
      "type": "story",
      "position": {
        "x": 960,
        "y": 165
      },
      "data": {
        "kind": "exit",
        "title": "Up in smoke",
        "description": "## Outcome\n\nThe Heron is burning (grain dust goes up like gunpowder) or the barge has gone down with the King's grain in her. Whatever the player didn't carry out is gone, the whole waterfront is awake, and on the eve of the Assembly somebody is going to have to explain it.\n\n## Closing\n\nClose on the spectacle, played absolutely straight: the light on the water, the bells, bargees swearing in Saltmere, Saul hauling Duchess clear, the Master's lavender lost in the smoke. Kell, soot on her notebook, says what she'll have to write.",
        "lore": [
          "Places/Heron Warehouse.md",
          "World/Caerwyn now.md",
          "World/Fronts.md"
        ],
        "sourceId": "up-in-smoke",
        "sourceFile": "scenes/heron-warehouse.ts",
        "sourceExit": {
          "id": "up-in-smoke",
          "kind": "other",
          "title": "Up in smoke",
          "next": "kings-morning",
          "outcome": "The Heron is burning (grain dust goes up like gunpowder) or the barge has gone down with the King's grain in her. Whatever the player didn't carry out is gone, the whole waterfront is awake, and on the eve of the Assembly somebody is going to have to explain it.",
          "closing": "Close on the spectacle, played absolutely straight: the light on the water, the bells, bargees swearing in Saltmere, Saul hauling Duchess clear, the Master's lavender lost in the smoke. Kell, soot on her notebook, says what she'll have to write.",
          "script": "(world, outcome) => {\n        if (has(outcome.established, FIRE)) {\n          world.place({ asset: world.assets.get(\"smoke-plume\"), at: world.anchor(\"heron-floor\") });\n          world.unsupported(\"The Heron warehouse burned down on the eve of the Assembly, with the King's grain in it.\");\n        }\n        if (has(outcome.established, SUNK)) world.unsupported(\"The Saltmere barge Patience sank at the Heron's wharf with the King's grain in her.\");\n        keepBook(world, outcome);\n        world.setFlag(\"true_book\", bookSaved(outcome) ? \"taken\" : \"burned\");\n        world.character(\"kell\").remember(\"The Heron went up in smoke (or its barge went down) on the eve of the Assembly, with the investigator in the middle of it. She'll have to write it up.\");\n        if (bookSaved(outcome)) world.quest(\"heron-ledger\").advance(\"up_in_smoke\", \"The Heron's grain is gone, but the true book came out with us.\");\n        else world.quest(\"heron-ledger\").fail(\"The Heron's grain and its true book went up in smoke or down in the river.\");\n        world.journal(\"The Heron's night ended in fire and water, and all Caerwyn saw it.\");\n      }"
        },
        "exitKind": "other",
        "next": "kings-morning",
        "file": "Scenes/The King's Morning.kmscene",
        "entry": "report",
        "destinationKind": "scene",
        "scriptSource": "(world, outcome) => {\n        if (has(outcome.established, FIRE)) {\n          world.place({ asset: world.assets.get(\"smoke-plume\"), at: world.anchor(\"heron-floor\") });\n          world.unsupported(\"The Heron warehouse burned down on the eve of the Assembly, with the King's grain in it.\");\n        }\n        if (has(outcome.established, SUNK)) world.unsupported(\"The Saltmere barge Patience sank at the Heron's wharf with the King's grain in her.\");\n        keepBook(world, outcome);\n        world.setFlag(\"true_book\", bookSaved(outcome) ? \"taken\" : \"burned\");\n        world.character(\"kell\").remember(\"The Heron went up in smoke (or its barge went down) on the eve of the Assembly, with the investigator in the middle of it. She'll have to write it up.\");\n        if (bookSaved(outcome)) world.quest(\"heron-ledger\").advance(\"up_in_smoke\", \"The Heron's grain is gone, but the true book came out with us.\");\n        else world.quest(\"heron-ledger\").fail(\"The Heron's grain and its true book went up in smoke or down in the river.\");\n        world.journal(\"The Heron's night ended in fire and water, and all Caerwyn saw it.\");\n      }"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "barge-sails",
      "type": "story",
      "position": {
        "x": 960,
        "y": 495
      },
      "data": {
        "kind": "exit",
        "title": "The barge sails",
        "description": "## Outcome\n\nThe Patience has cast off on the ebb with the King's grain aboard (and anything Sallow sent with her), and is away downriver into the dark. By morning the Heron will be swept and empty. Whatever the player holds, they hold; the rest is gone.\n\n## Closing\n\nClose on the barge's stern lantern dwindling down the black river, the bargees singing, and the Heron's doors swinging shut. Let Kell say one dry thing, and leave the player on the wharf with whatever they have.",
        "lore": [
          "Places/Heron Warehouse.md",
          "World/Caerwyn now.md",
          "World/Fronts.md"
        ],
        "sourceId": "barge-sails",
        "sourceFile": "scenes/heron-warehouse.ts",
        "sourceExit": {
          "id": "barge-sails",
          "kind": "leave",
          "title": "The barge sails",
          "next": "kings-morning",
          "outcome": "The Patience has cast off on the ebb with the King's grain aboard (and anything Sallow sent with her), and is away downriver into the dark. By morning the Heron will be swept and empty. Whatever the player holds, they hold; the rest is gone.",
          "closing": "Close on the barge's stern lantern dwindling down the black river, the bargees singing, and the Heron's doors swinging shut. Let Kell say one dry thing, and leave the player on the wharf with whatever they have.",
          "script": "(world, outcome) => {\n        keepBook(world, outcome);\n        bookFlag(world, outcome);\n        if (!bookSaved(outcome)) world.quest(\"heron-ledger\").fail(\"The Patience sailed with the King's grain before we could stop her.\");\n        world.journal(\"The Patience sailed on the ebb with the King's grain aboard.\");\n      }"
        },
        "exitKind": "leave",
        "next": "kings-morning",
        "file": "Scenes/The King's Morning.kmscene",
        "entry": "report",
        "destinationKind": "scene",
        "scriptSource": "(world, outcome) => {\n        keepBook(world, outcome);\n        bookFlag(world, outcome);\n        if (!bookSaved(outcome)) world.quest(\"heron-ledger\").fail(\"The Patience sailed with the King's grain before we could stop her.\");\n        world.journal(\"The Patience sailed on the ebb with the King's grain aboard.\");\n      }"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "fight",
      "type": "story",
      "position": {
        "x": 960,
        "y": 825
      },
      "data": {
        "kind": "exit",
        "title": "Roll for initiative",
        "description": "## Outcome\n\nA fight breaks out in the Heron between the player (and Kell, if she's with them) and whoever is on the floor to fight them: Master Sallow with his sword-cane and the Crakes, if he has come; if he hasn't come yet, Hep and her gang, with their knives and sack-needles, and Sallow and the Crakes aren't in it. It's in the grain dust and the swinging lantern light.\n\n## Closing\n\nClose on the moment the fight breaks out, with whoever is on the floor to fight it. If Master Sallow has come (he's here, a minute behind his lavender), his cane slides apart into a thin bright sword and the Crakes roll their shoulders. If he hasn't come yet, he isn't in this and doesn't come in now: Hep's gang put down their sacks and come with their knives and sack-needles, Hep bellowing them on. Either way: the dust in the lantern light, the lanterns swinging dangerously close to it, and anyone with any sense stepping smartly out of the way. End with 'Roll for initiative!'",
        "lore": [
          "Places/Heron Warehouse.md",
          "World/Caerwyn now.md",
          "World/Fronts.md"
        ],
        "sourceId": "fight",
        "sourceFile": "scenes/heron-warehouse.ts",
        "sourceExit": {
          "id": "fight",
          "kind": "combat",
          "title": "Roll for initiative",
          "next": "kings-morning",
          "outcome": "A fight breaks out in the Heron between the player (and Kell, if she's with them) and whoever is on the floor to fight them: Master Sallow with his sword-cane and the Crakes, if he has come; if he hasn't come yet, Hep and her gang, with their knives and sack-needles, and Sallow and the Crakes aren't in it. It's in the grain dust and the swinging lantern light.",
          "closing": "Close on the moment the fight breaks out, with whoever is on the floor to fight it. If Master Sallow has come (he's here, a minute behind his lavender), his cane slides apart into a thin bright sword and the Crakes roll their shoulders. If he hasn't come yet, he isn't in this and doesn't come in now: Hep's gang put down their sacks and come with their knives and sack-needles, Hep bellowing them on. Either way: the dust in the lantern light, the lanterns swinging dangerously close to it, and anyone with any sense stepping smartly out of the way. End with 'Roll for initiative!'",
          "script": "(world, outcome) => {\n        world.startCombat({\n          enemies: has(outcome.established, MASTER_HERE)\n            ? [{ asset: world.assets.get(\"bandit\"), count: 2, leader: \"sallow\" }]\n            : [{ asset: world.assets.get(\"bandit\"), count: 6, leader: \"hep\" }],\n          allies: [\"kell\"],\n          at: world.anchor(\"heron-floor\"),\n        });\n      }"
        },
        "exitKind": "combat",
        "next": "kings-morning",
        "file": "Scenes/The King's Morning.kmscene",
        "entry": "report",
        "destinationKind": "scene",
        "scriptSource": "(world, outcome) => {\n        world.startCombat({\n          enemies: has(outcome.established, MASTER_HERE)\n            ? [{ asset: world.assets.get(\"bandit\"), count: 2, leader: \"sallow\" }]\n            : [{ asset: world.assets.get(\"bandit\"), count: 6, leader: \"hep\" }],\n          allies: [\"kell\"],\n          at: world.anchor(\"heron-floor\"),\n        });\n      }"
      }
    }
  ],
