      "data": {
        "condition": "Sallow has been caught at the loading of the King's grain before witnesses who will swear to it (Kell, Hep's gang, Scrope, Hobb or the player), Kell has arrested him, and he is actually held: he has given himself up (the cane handed over, his hands up) or been beaten or overpowered, and his Crakes have stood down or been dealt with. The words of arrest alone, with Sallow defiant and his Crakes still beside him, aren't this: that is the moment he draws.",
